    <fr:title text="Constructing Equalizers in Type Theory">Constructing Equalizers in Type Theory</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <fr:p>In the presence of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Sigma ]]></fr:tex>-types, one may construct all <fr:link href="sss-001L.xml" title="Equalizer" addr="sss-001L" type="local">equalizers</fr:link>. Given types <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex> with functions <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f, g : A \to  B]]></fr:tex>, the equalizer may be constructed as
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\mathsf {eq}_{f,g} \colonequals  \mathchoice {\textstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (a : A\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\textstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (a : A\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\scriptstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (a : A\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\scriptscriptstyle \sum _{{\mathopen {}\left (a : A\right )\mathclose {}}}}{{\mathopen {}\left (f(a) = g(a)\right )\mathclose {}}}]]></fr:tex></fr:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
